{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/909519-two-sides-of-every-clan","id":909519,"title":"Two Sides of Every Clan","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-07T15:30:03-07:00","id":909519,"title":"Two Sides of Every Clan","content":"In my current setting we are trying out a new concept where every clan has two sides.<br /> <br /> For example:<br /> <br /> Gangrel being the wanders and roams of the world of darkness we gave them the Spirit discipline found in the BOS as a fourth Discipline.<br /> <br /> So at character creation the player picks Protean or Tenebrous then they get the other two clan Vigor and Resilience disciplines as &quot;in clan&quot;. Where a kindred reaches a certain level of Blood Potency (we're thinking 3 or 4) they unlock the discipline they didn't choose at character creation as in clan, but aren't compelled to purchase it of course unless they like.<br /> <br /> Nosferatu being Haunts and having a ghost theme choose NIghtmare or Essentiaphagia (though we've been considering making a costume Discipline based off the Sin Eaters Marionette + Stigmata ghost abilities. Input requested for balance)<br /> <br /> Mekhet being Shadows get Auspex or Obenbration. I would like input on how to use the Discipline in 2.0 I saw the update used all devotions. Would like suggestions on making it a regular discipline<br /> <br /> Deava and Ventru I'm running into an issue of what there other side discipline should be. Unless I change their disciplines enough to make them the other side of each other, effectively being the same Clan, but I don't much like that idea.<br /> <br /> Also I wanted to make <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Praestantia </span></span>discipline that pumps Dex a main stream discipline, not some strange rare one. It just makes sense to have a buff for all three physical stats.<br /> <br /> I considered removing Vigor of Celirity from Deava and giving it to them as a common discipline, but following the rule of common disciplines I wanted to give it to one of the other clans as well. I'd like input.<br /> <br /> To recap.<br /> <br /> Input on using Essentiaphagia or another ghost discipline for Nosferatu to them a ghost side of the Clan.<br /> <br /> Input on Obtenbration as a discipline instead of a devotion <br /> <br /> Input on a 4th Discpline for Deava and Ventru or making them the other side of each other<br /> <br /> Input on making <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Praestantia </span></span>a common discipline among vampire instead of being exotic and how to make it VTR 2.0 balanced <br /> <br /> Thank you in advance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2191-kevorkiandoctor","name":"Kevorkiandoctor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T18:24:55-07:00","id":909673,"title":"","content":"About Praestentia, be careful that it doesn't make firearms overpowered. Sure, you can't do lethal with them, but they ignore normal defense and unless you make sure to fight in an area with decent cover or you have celerity, you usually don't get any defense at all. Of course if firearms are hard to come by and attract enough attention when used, it could discourage their use enough that it would be fair.<br /> <br /> About obtenebration, well, I don't know, but making it a really common discipline seems a bit of a bummer. To me, it's always been that discipline that was supposed to look completely useless (shaping shadows ? great so what ?) except from the really high levels where you teleport and turn into a shadow (and really, if it's for stealth, obfuscate does a better job). The trick is nobody really knows what its purpose is. There are khaibit out there and they know how to use it (and can teach it since it's not restricted to the bloodline, just really rare and weird) but mostly don't know what it could be used FOR, namely, fighting strix on equal ground. Shaping shadows could be used to strike as strix or block their path/grapple them, shadow jump emulates the strix shadow jump and shadow form straight up allows you to step into the strix's arena and punch them in the beak.<br /> <br /> I like Khaibit/obtenebration users as unwitting possessors of one of the few powers that can really hurt and stop the strix, but instead use them for other jobs because they don't know better. Making it a mainstream discipline means vampires have a direct and easily accessible weapon at their disposal to fight the strix (well, you know, one that doesn't also causes you to frenzy and burn). It also means the Mekhet can bargain for a lot if strix activity is detected, since they're the most competent to deal with the problem.<br /> <br /> Seems like a decent idea, aside from that (to me). Blood tenebrous is a pretty fun discipline and Gangrel as a shaman clan seems nice. It would definitely put them in a special position with werewolves. Ghost eating discipline gives an interesting twist to nosferatu too, that sounds pretty good. Daeva and Ventrue, I don't know. Maybe for Ventrue, try Gilded Cage and make it a discipline instead of a magic (it is supposed to be exclusive to a ventrue bloodline anyway). I think it conveys well the idea of power that can represent the ventrue.<br /> <br /> Thing is, if you start giving blood tenebrous and essentiaphagia to two clans, you effectively start giving them tools to interact with another part of reality and other creatures. In that way, I guess obetenebration is appropriate (the problem is that the creatures in this case mostly hate your guts). I think it's a good theme to go about, so the question is what other aspect of the world of darkness should daeva and ventrue have a unique perspective on ? To go back to gilded cage, power over the city, use of ley lines and stuff, maybe it's use is actually a way for ventrue to unwittingly tamper into the god machine's work. Maybe the way it works is that it hijacks infrastructures. The ventrue think they're doing feng shui or that architecture is a vessel for power, but when they conduct a ritual or influence an architect's plans to suit their needs, they're actually rearranging the cogs of the machinery. Most of them don't know they're doing that and don't know about the god machine, and the discipline's use is usually too small scale or incidental to be noticed as tampering by the god machine. If a lot of ventrue started using that power without restraint, though, it could draw the attantion of angels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T19:42:39-07:00","id":909750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/909519-two-sides-of-every-clan?p=909673#post909673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About Praestentia, be careful that it doesn't make firearms overpowered. Sure, you can't do lethal with them, but they ignore normal defense and unless you make sure to fight in an area with decent cover or you have celerity, you usually don't get any defense at all. Of course if firearms are hard to come by and attract enough attention when used, it could discourage their use enough that it would be fair.</div> </div> </div> </div> That is a fair worry, but I've seen characters with vigor rip kindred's arms off or throw them threw walls, so I think it's about balanced. Do you have any ideas of the secondary effects it should have<br /> <br /> Passive: Add to Dex<br /> <br /> Spend a Viate: Auto success like Vigor?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/909519-two-sides-of-every-clan?p=909673#post909673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> About obtenebration, well, I don't know, but making it a really common discipline seems a bit of a bummer.</div> </div> </div> </div> It would still be a clan specific discpline like to clan Mekhet, it wouldn't be considered common like <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Praestantia, Vigor, Reslience, or Celerity. </span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/909519-two-sides-of-every-clan?p=909673#post909673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To go back to gilded cage, power over the city, use of ley lines and stuff, maybe it's use is actually a way for ventrue to unwittingly tamper into the god machine's work. Maybe the way it works is that it hijacks infrastructures. The ventrue think they're doing feng shui or that architecture is a vessel for power, but when they conduct a ritual or influence an architect's plans to suit their needs, they're actually rearranging the cogs of the machinery. Most of them don't know they're doing that and don't know about the god machine, and the discipline's use is usually too small scale or incidental to be noticed as tampering by the god machine. If a lot of ventrue started using that power without restraint, though, it could draw the attantion of angels.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like this idea!<br /> <br /> Any ideas for Deava's other side of the Clan Discpline? Or at least something to help me narrow it down?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2191-kevorkiandoctor","name":"Kevorkiandoctor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T04:39:58-07:00","id":909972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kevorkiandoctor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/909519-two-sides-of-every-clan#post909519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To recap.<br /> <br /> Input on using Essentiaphagia or another ghost discipline for Nosferatu to them a ghost side of the Clan.<br /> <br /> Input on Obtenbration as a discipline instead of a devotion<br /> <br /> Input on a 4th Discpline for Deava and Ventru or making them the other side of each other</div> </div> </div> </div> You basically have what I like to call the Mage situation. One splat manipulates spirits (thyrsus), another ghosts (moros) and one that attacks them all (obrimos). This creates a situation where, in order to attack your enemies, it all comes down to what ephemeral forces you call up to attack them, and how they're defended against.<br /> <br /> Remember, spirits and ghosts can't interact with each other, but they can absolutely Blast Numina a vampire from Twilight. There's no defense for someone without some way to interact with Twilight. For &quot;the other side&quot; you've effectively forced all vampires to interact with ephemeral beings in some way, or die a messy death with no defense.<br /> <br /> You are also going to need to consider if vampires will be able to detect spirits through Predator's Aura. Otherwise, we're dealing with super spies everywhere that can act unobserved. But I've gotten off the main point I was trying to make. Because of this &quot;everyone's got ephemeral power&quot; theme of the first three, that's going to have to inform your second two clans. Without it, the game is simply too lopsided, and any confrontation is going to unfairly weigh in the balance of those with ephemeral powers than those without.<br /> <br /> If you use Gilded Cage = Infrastructure, then you can basically use angels for Ventrue as the third ephemeral. This leaves goetics as the last possible entity for Deava to keep anything resembling balance here.<br /> <br /> Also, you want Obtenebration a five rank disipline? There's five powers already. Just put them in order, and done.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Input on making <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Praestantia </span></span>a common discipline among vampire instead of being exotic and how to make it VTR 2.0 balanced<br /> <br /> Thank you in advance! </div> </div> </div> Praestantia can merely be a Vigor/Celerity devotion. In truth, Praestantia basically was a scene long version of the Hair Trigger devotion, which, in itself, was basically a turn-length Vigor boost. There's no reason for Praestantia to be a full discipline when the only benefit it will provide is pretty much already covered under Vigor or Celerity; all you need is a little twist on those two, allowing Dex boost and some weapon bonus to ranged weaponry.<br /> <br /> What I would do is basically this:<br /> <br /> Manus<br /> (Quicken Sight, Vigor o)<br /> Hand-eye coordination can be tricky for many people, requiring far more than training muscles. However, by combining the speed of Celerity, enhanced senses of the Beast, and the muscle control of Vigor, a vampire can create a temporary shortcut.<br /> Cost: 1 vitae<br /> Dice Pool: None<br /> Action: Reflexive<br /> When activating Quicken Sight, you may add your dots in Vigor to your Dexterity instead of your Strength for the turn. Any weapon attacks gain Vigor dots as an equipment bonus; you may spend further Vitae to use other aspects of Vigor, Celerity or the Quicken Sight devotion as well.<br /> This Devotion costs 1 Experiences to learn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-08-2016, 07:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T05:22:49-07:00","id":909985,"title":"","content":"Praesantia also allowed for precognition flashes of imminent failure which allowed the user to reroll failed rolls. They also get clairaudience flashes of conversation whenever someone speaks the name Shaddad. It doesn't seem that impressive but it can be turned into an effective tool of telepathic communication between praesantia users.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T05:37:49-07:00","id":909994,"title":"","content":"For Daeva, looking at the list of requiem disciplines, the one that may be the most appropriate and with potential ramifications could be Ars Speculorum. It's a discipline that lets one use mirrrors in various ways. Level 2 lets you ask a question to something and get a cryptic answer, level 3 lets you see out of various mirrors and 5 lets you travel via mirrors. It's in the book &quot;mythologies&quot; and it's supposed to be granted by a spirit/ghost named red jack that appears in mirrors. You could rule that they came up with it on their own, though. I think the mirror theme is appropriate to Daevas, being the prototypical seductive vampires and stuff. Finally, there's also the question of what they're actually doing when they interact with mirrors, and where they're going when they step into them (you spend some time in a weird place when you travel between two mirrors). The book hints at a spirit, but it could also be that, like some Alice, they actually manage temporary tunnels through Arcadia. When they use that level 5 powers, the true fae would sometimes see a glimpse of a humanoid figure going through one of their mirrors. What would happen if they try to reach throuh it ? Would the vampire in the mirror dimension see a hand appear in their way ?<br /> <br /> It would also cause weird dynamics with changelings. Chagnelings who would learn of that power and start having an idea what Daevas are actually doing could react differently. A summer court could ask, more or less politely, the vampire to help them. They could try to follow him so they could break into a true fae's domain to rescue other changeling or have the vampire repeatedly travel between two mirrors i hopes that it would eventually lure a fae outside, where they prepared a big trap. A winter court could see this power as a major threat and think it's onnly a matter of time until a curious fae (really, many of them) follows the vampire back to the city and starts wreaking havoc for the changeling. Of course, the whole reason this discipline exists could also be because it was given to the daeva long ago by a true fae. Every time it is used, that fae can see through the mirror (a bit like the Strangers in 7th Sea) and look for potential new victims to abduct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T06:35:41-07:00","id":910026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/909519-two-sides-of-every-clan?p=909985#post909985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Praesantia also allowed for precognition flashes of imminent failure which allowed the user to reroll failed rolls. They also get clairaudience flashes of conversation whenever someone speaks the name Shaddad. It doesn't seem that impressive but it can be turned into an effective tool of telepathic communication between praesantia users.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm separating it from clan VII so I think I'll drop that second part off, but thanks for reminding me of the precognition. <br /> <br /> So would you reckon the three levels of the Power<br /> <br /> Passive: add to dex<br /> <br /> Passive: know if you'll fail the role <br /> <br /> Activate: powerful success like vigor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2191-kevorkiandoctor","name":"Kevorkiandoctor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T06:38:49-07:00","id":910027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/909519-two-sides-of-every-clan?p=909972#post909972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You basically have what I like to call the Mage situation. One splat manipulates spirits (thyrsus), another ghosts (moros) and one that attacks them all (obrimos). This creates a situation where, in order to attack your enemies, it all comes down to what ephemeral forces you call up to attack them, and how they're defended against.<br /> <br /> Remember, spirits and ghosts can't interact with each other, but they can absolutely Blast Numina a vampire from Twilight. There's no defense for someone without some way to interact with Twilight. For &amp;quot;the other side&amp;quot; you've effectively forced all vampires to interact with ephemeral beings in some way, or die a messy death with no defense.</div> </div> </div> </div>So far I've considered a devotion for the Gilded Cage and resilience to strengthen the gauntlet/make it harder for entities to use powers on the physical world.<br /> <br /> But do you think that mirroring Mage would unbalance the game/that Mage is unbalanced ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2191-kevorkiandoctor","name":"Kevorkiandoctor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T07:07:18-07:00","id":910049,"title":"","content":"That's a good concern, but in terms of discipline, blood tenebrous doesn't allow one to &quot;manipulate&quot; spirits. It only allows a vampire to interact with spirits and the spirit wold. It doesn't turn a vampire using it into a master of spirits. I mean, werewolves have a lot more options to deal with spirits and they don't manipulate them. At best, they can make deals or trap them and their relationship with them is antagonistic as often as it is peaceful. Having blood tenebrous for a vampire, in my mind, only allows them to realize that the world has an unseen side most people aren't aware of. They're messing with something they don't fully understand. Sure, they can deal with spirits, mostly by turning their vitae into essence to pay them, but that's a costly power and a vampire doesn't just throw essence around like candy. Honestly, I think a vampire using blood tenebrous is just as likely to gain something from dealing with spirits as it is to attract unwanted attention from more powerful spirits that will see them as a potential source of essence to be captures/exploited. And that's not even taking werewolves into account. A vampire messing with spirits will eventually be noticed by werewolves who will want to know who's causing it. What happens next depends on how responsibly the vampire is dealing with spirits (and wether the werewolves are forsaken or pure), but if werewolves usually try to keep humans from knowing too much about spirits, I don't know if they'd like knowing vampires can interact with them.<br /> <br /> Going by the same idea, nosferatu will be noticed by Geist, and Mekhet, possessing one of the few reliable weapons that can hurt the strix would probably be targeted early by them when they come around.<br /> <br /> Going by the idea ventrue tamper with the god machine, if you assume that can allow them to indirectly manipulate angels, that would defenitely not earn them the good favors of the god machine when it finds out. Demons might find that interesting but they're more likely to try and manipulate a ventrue from the shadows (using him to sabotage the GM's plans and then letting him suffer the consequences) than they are to openly propose an alliance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T09:08:12-07:00","id":910121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kevorkiandoctor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/909519-two-sides-of-every-clan?p=910027#post910027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So far I've considered a devotion for the Gilded Cage and resilience to strengthen the gauntlet/make it harder for entities to use powers on the physical world.<br /> <br /> But do you think that mirroring Mage would unbalance the game/that Mage is unbalanced ?</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, its not so much &quot;broken&quot; that I'm wondering about so much as that you're going to end up with a shift in the mindset of the game. Vampire, as a whole, isn't really set up to handle threats from Twilight or other realms; we saw this a lot whenever a game used the alternative Hisil summoning rituals in the CotC book. Simply put, no vampire was a match for a spirit swarm. This created a completely new dynamic whenever someone interacted with the Circle - &quot;do we stand a chance here if we piss them off?&quot; Generally, my players went with &quot;nope!&quot; Things became less interesting in the game as a result.<br /> <br /> My biggest point is that we'd have a cold war situation where no one would be willing to face the threat of what ammouts to spirit-armegeddon on themselves. You won't fear the guy with big Aura, you'll fear the unseen ephemeral armies. Is this the kind of thing that you want in your game?<br /> <br /> As well, given that spirit Influences can do pretty much anything, will there be as much appeal for Covenant bonuses, or will there be a move for Clan-based games, given solidarity? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/909519-two-sides-of-every-clan?p=910049#post910049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a good concern, but in terms of discipline, blood tenebrous doesn't allow one to &quot;manipulate&quot; spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div> It exactly lets you manipulate spirits, because you have practically infinite access to their all consuming drive - free essence. Spirits can be targets of Social Maneuvering, they can be taken as Retainers and Allies. Futhermore, Dominate and other disciplines still work on spirits, so compelling their actions is still on the table as well.<br /> <br /> Blood Tenebros was designed to let a vampire work inside of a Hisil-based game, not to bring spirits into a Vampire-based game. Ephemerals of all kinds are absolutely are a major game changer, and will fundamentally alter how the game works. Mind you, I'm not saying this is a bad thing, but be warned that it absolutely will have an effect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And that's not even taking werewolves into account. </div> </div> </div> I'm not comfortable assuming werewolves exist in this game. That's something the OP will have to decide on their own - the only games that assume crossover are Hunter and Beast.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A vampire messing with spirits will eventually be noticed by werewolves who will want to know who's causing it. What happens next depends on how responsibly the vampire is dealing with spirits (and wether the werewolves are forsaken or pure), but if werewolves usually try to keep humans from knowing too much about spirits, I don't know if they'd like knowing vampires can interact with them.<br /> <br /> Going by the same idea, nosferatu will be noticed by Geist, and Mekhet, possessing one of the few reliable weapons that can hurt the strix would probably be targeted early by them when they come around.<br /> <br /> Going by the idea ventrue tamper with the god machine, if you assume that can allow them to indirectly manipulate angels, that would defenitely not earn them the good favors of the god machine when it finds out. Demons might find that interesting but they're more likely to try and manipulate a ventrue from the shadows (using him to sabotage the GM's plans and then letting him suffer the consequences) than they are to openly propose an alliance. </div> </div> </div> And if we do have all this crossover, we're basically sentencing the game to being a crossover bananza instead of a Vampire game. Is that desirable for the OP? Is this the kind of game that they want?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-08-2016, 12:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T09:56:57-07:00","id":910147,"title":"","content":"Werewolves do exist in the world, but there aren't any in this city. There is legends of them and tales to stay out of Lumberton (a city a few towns over) <br /> <br /> I do understand that allowing a clan like Ganges to affect spirits does shift the mood a bit. Nosferatu dealing with Ghost fits into a vampire game, but spirits opens the game up more and adds new dynamics that I think all the other splat get to enjoy.<br /> <br /> I think a balance for the discipline is that spirits are hungry and greedy as warned with essence blood merit. A spirit might get greedy and try to eat you to get all the essence it assumes you're holding back. Spirits aren't human minded or even animal minded they are other minded and if you keep dangling yourself out there as a source of essence you'll become a target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2191-kevorkiandoctor","name":"Kevorkiandoctor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T10:10:53-07:00","id":910159,"title":"","content":"In short, you can invest in the Discipline, but it will absolutely bite you in the ass? Putting aside the Hisil, are you planning on doing the same thing for ghosts and angels, who'll object to messign with Infrastructure? How do you balance it? How will players feel about being a ticking time bomb?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T10:24:08-07:00","id":910170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/909519-two-sides-of-every-clan?p=910159#post910159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In short, you can invest in the Discipline, but it will absolutely bite you in the ass? Putting aside the Hisil, are you planning on doing the same thing for ghosts and angels, who'll object to messign with Infrastructure? How do you balance it? How will players feel about being a ticking time bomb?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about Angels being affected and manipulated yet, but I don't think the disciplines spirit or ghost will guaranteed that it'll bite you in the ass. Just the nature of the creatures when you manipulate them enough tends to bite you","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2191-kevorkiandoctor","name":"Kevorkiandoctor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T10:24:41-07:00","id":910172,"title":"","content":"Kind how Dominate fluff wise says that it drives mortals insane over time","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2191-kevorkiandoctor","name":"Kevorkiandoctor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T13:12:00-07:00","id":910270,"title":"","content":"I really don't think blood tenebrous gives you that much control over spirits. Sure you can ue social skills on them (I'm leaving out social maneuvering because no) and dominate them (although isn't there a penalty for using that on a spirit, and gangrels don't get dominate in clan), but anybody can do that as long as they know they're around and they're willing to show themselves.<br /> <br /> And let's take into account the cost of turning your blood into essence. It costs one willpower and you turn some of you own vitae into as many essence. We're not talking about an infinite source of essence here, we're talking about a vampire who must hunt more than usual to have something to put on the table when bargaining with spirits. And then there's the question of how much essence spirits will ask for. I don't know it is in other people's games, but I'm playing in a werewolf game and I usually have to pay like 2 to 3 essence to convince some crow spirits to go spy on someone. This is just basic spying for like two or three days. Keep in mind that if a spirit needs to use some of their powers, they'll definitely ask for the corresponding essence. You can't just pay a spirit 2 essence and expect it to go blast your daeva rival into torpor.<br /> <br /> Besides, no, spirits don't just want essence, they want to cross over to the human world, they want to possess people, they want to have fun as spirits do, and blood tenebrous doesn't have a direct way to stop that, just a way to go and try to negotiate for them to stop. It's all fun and games with a spirit of good health, but if a spirit of pain or death starts having its way in the human world, this is going to cause problems. And again, a really powerful spirit might be convinced to act once or twice for the vampire, but if they really see them as, like you said, an infinite source of essence, they're just as likely to start thinking they should just abduct them and feed them humans to have an essence bank at the ready.<br /> <br /> At the same time, I wouldn't call it a &quot;ticking time bomb&quot;, I mean let's not be completely pessimistic here. The GM is the one who decides stuff. What it means, though is that a vampire who practices blood tenebrous has to be careful what he does with it. Bargain with spirits that it knows aren't so powerful that they'll easily destroy him, not overuse it so that it won't look like an essence open bar has opened and be careful how much essence your throw around because that is vitae, the same precious vitae that you use to activate resilience and wake up in the evening.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T15:07:51-07:00","id":910348,"title":"","content":"On the subject of Prestantia, I would personally suggest just modifying Celerity. It sounds like what you want is to have three physical Disciplines that each passively boost one of the three physical Attributes and actively do something else for combat. Vigor passively boosts Strength and actively adds to damage. Resilience passively boosts Stamina and actively adds to armor. Why not have Celerity passively boost Dexterity and actively add to Defense? Keep the initiative jumping and speed multiplying abilities and you won't need to muck around with the precognition thing that ends up being awkward in play with dice re-roll mechanics and such, and no need to add damage to Fierarms attacks which ends up being overpowered. And as a bonus, you don't have to change any Clan Discipline spreads to account for the addition of a 4th physical Discipline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T15:21:30-07:00","id":910358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/909519-two-sides-of-every-clan?p=910348#post910348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the subject of Prestantia, I would personally suggest just modifying Celerity. It sounds like what you want is to have three physical Disciplines that each passively boost one of the three physical Attributes and actively do something else for combat. Vigor passively boosts Strength and actively adds to damage. Resilience passively boosts Stamina and actively adds to armor. Why not have Celerity passively boost Dexterity and actively add to Defense? Keep the initiative jumping and speed multiplying abilities and you won't need to muck around with the precognition thing that ends up being awkward in play with dice re-roll mechanics and such, and no need to add damage to Fierarms attacks which ends up being overpowered. And as a bonus, you don't have to change any Clan Discipline spreads to account for the addition of a 4th physical Discipline.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I really like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2191-kevorkiandoctor","name":"Kevorkiandoctor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}